[16.531273, "o", "59:matching capabilities (*note Regular expressions::).\r\n148:<newline> character. Commands beginning with '#' are taken as comments and\r\n249:3 Invoking ed\r\n329:   Exit status: 0 if no errors occurred; otherwise >0.\r\n331:4 Line addressing\r\n355:   Addresses can be omitted on either side of the comma or semicolon\r\n415:   Addresses can be followed by one or more address offsets, optionally\r\n433:5 Regular expressions\r\n436:Regular expressions are patterns used in selecting text. For example, the\r\n441:prints all lines containing STRING. Regular expressions are also used by\r\n583:6 Commands\r\n656:     Global command. The global command makes two passes over the file. On\r\n867:7 Substitute command\r\n955:9 Diagnostics\r\n978:Node: Invoking ed11584\r\n980:Node: Regular expressions18529\r\n981:Node: Commands24714\r\n986:Node: Diagnostics42163\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@162cc866fc92:/app# "]
